Add a provider source, then sync it to archive its messages or contacts.
Start by choosing the provider below. Gmail, IMAP and Microsoft mail use
'msgvault sync'; chat, calendar and meeting providers use their own sync action.

Local exports use 'msgvault import <format>'. List registered sources and
their IDs with 'msgvault account list --json'.

Usage:
  msgvault source [command]

Examples:
  msgvault source gmail add you@gmail.com
  msgvault sync-full you@gmail.com
  msgvault account list --json

Available Commands:
  beeper             Archive chats exposed by Beeper Desktop
  calendar           Archive Google Calendar events with OAuth
  carddav            Sync CardDAV, Google and Microsoft contacts
  chatwoot           Archive Chatwoot inbox conversations and calls
  circleback         Archive Circleback meetings and action items
  discord            Archive Discord guilds with a bot token
  facebook-comments  Archive comments from a configured Facebook Page
  gmail              Archive Gmail mail with Google OAuth
  granola            Archive Granola meeting notes and transcripts
  imap               Archive mail from an IMAP server
  inline             Archive Inline chats with read-only authorization
  instagram-comments Archive comments from a linked Instagram account
  matrix             Archive Matrix rooms with a read-only device
  muesli             Archive meetings from a local Muesli database
  notion-meetings    Archive Notion AI Meeting Notes
  o365               Archive Microsoft 365 or Outlook.com mail
  omi                Archive Omi meeting conversations and transcripts
  plaud              Archive Plaud cloud transcripts and notes
  pocket             Archive Pocket meeting transcripts and summaries
  slack              Archive Slack workspaces with a user token
  synctech-sms       Archive SMS Backup & Restore files from Google Drive
  teams              Archive Microsoft Teams chats with Microsoft OAuth
  twenty             Archive Twenty Call Recorder meetings
  twilio             Archive Twilio calls, recordings and transcripts

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for source

Global Flags: --agent-allow-insecure, --agent-token-file, --agent-url, --config, --home, --local, --log-file, --log-level, --log-sql, --log-sql-slow-ms, --no-log-file, -v/--verbose (see 'msgvault --help')

Use "msgvault source [command] --help" for more information about a command.
